# MagFace®

> MagFace® is a patented dry magnetic installation system for floors and walls. A 1 mm magnetic layer on the back of each porcelain tile or slab lets porcelain stoneware, natural stone and decorative surfaces be installed without adhesive, removed and reused. Developed by Bassi Group International Srl (Castelnovo di Sotto, Reggio Emilia, Italy), active in magnetic systems since 2002. International patent 2015. Founder and inventor: Andrea Bassi.

## Key facts
- Technology: dry magnetic installation (Italian: posa magnetica a secco); no adhesive, no demolition, surfaces can be replaced and reused.
- Formats: slabs up to 160×320 cm.
- Tests and classifications: Heavy Duty, Robinson Test ASTM C627-10; reaction to fire EN 13501-1; self-extinguishing UL 94.
- Audience: architects, designers, contractors, distributors, ceramic manufacturers, professional installers (B2B).
- Licensing: Bronze, Silver and Gold levels for ceramic and stone manufacturers.
- Training: MagFace Academy (dry magnetic installation, cutting and drilling of slabs, joint finishing with MagFiller®).
- Reference project: MagFace® Concept House (2018, 110 m², 24 hours, no invasive demolition).

